# mbsync (isync 1.5) — two IMAP accounts, full history, maildirs under ~/.mail/.
# Decided in emacs-l88, executed in emacs-l7d (ray-a-m/emacs beads).
#
# Secrets come from the GNOME keyring (secret-tool), never from this file.
# Store them once per machine:
#   secret-tool store --label="mail fastmail" service mail account fastmail
#   secret-tool store --label="mail gmail"    service mail account gmail
#
# Fallback note (do not build until needed): if Google ever kills app
# passwords, Gmail moves to XOAUTH2 via oama or mutt_oauth2.py.

# Global channel defaults — apply to every channel below.
Create Both
Expunge Both
SyncState *
CopyArrivalDate yes

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fastmail

IMAPAccount fastmail
Host imap.fastmail.com
Port 993
User ray@raymondmaung.com
PassCmd "secret-tool lookup service mail account fastmail"
TLSType IMAPS

IMAPStore fastmail-remote
Account fastmail

MaildirStore fastmail-local
Path ~/.mail/fastmail/
Inbox ~/.mail/fastmail/INBOX
SubFolders Verbatim

# Everything, Spam included — full history is the point.
Channel fastmail
Far :fastmail-remote:
Near :fastmail-local:
Patterns *

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Gmail

IMAPAccount gmail
Host imap.gmail.com
Port 993
User ronokaoswe@gmail.com
PassCmd "secret-tool lookup service mail account gmail"
TLSType IMAPS

IMAPStore gmail-remote
Account gmail

MaildirStore gmail-local
Path ~/.mail/gmail/
Inbox ~/.mail/gmail/INBOX
SubFolders Verbatim

# One channel per folder, so the local names lose the "[Gmail]/" prefix.
# All Mail is where archived mail lives — without it, history has holes.

Channel gmail-inbox
Far :gmail-remote:INBOX
Near :gmail-local:INBOX

Channel gmail-all
Far :gmail-remote:"[Gmail]/All Mail"
Near :gmail-local:"All Mail"

Channel gmail-sent
Far :gmail-remote:"[Gmail]/Sent Mail"
Near :gmail-local:"Sent"

Channel gmail-drafts
Far :gmail-remote:"[Gmail]/Drafts"
Near :gmail-local:"Drafts"

Channel gmail-spam
Far :gmail-remote:"[Gmail]/Spam"
Near :gmail-local:"Spam"

Channel gmail-trash
Far :gmail-remote:"[Gmail]/Trash"
Near :gmail-local:"Trash"

Group gmail
Channel gmail-inbox
Channel gmail-all
Channel gmail-sent
Channel gmail-drafts
Channel gmail-spam
Channel gmail-trash
